2026-07-09T18:25:08.3650259Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3650739Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3651257Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3651470Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3651741Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3651953Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3652191Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3652413Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3652690Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3652923Z             return x + 1
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3653164Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3653367Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3653571Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3653827Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3654074Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3654270Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3654466Z     To execute it::
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3654674Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3654867Z         $ pytest
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3655165Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3655531Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3655773Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3656184Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3656427Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3656689Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3656863Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3656952Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657051Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657158Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657263Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657362Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657453Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657569Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657732Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657823Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3657906Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3658623Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3658864Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3658950Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659048Z     Features
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659147Z     --------
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659233Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659714Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659807Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3659913Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660230Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660348Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660433Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660704Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660886Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3660982Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3661364Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3661480Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3661567Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3661681Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3661771Z     
2026-07-09T18:25:08.3662227Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
